## Alternatives Comparisons

### Deployment Platform Alternatives

- [Qovery vs Vercel](https://www.qovery.com/alternatives/vercel): Vercel runs your application on Vercel's infrastructure, shaped around frontend and serverless workloads. Qovery gives agents the same one-command deploy against your own AWS, GCP, Azure or Scaleway account, with managed databases, background workers, Helm charts and Kubernetes workloads inside your VPC. The qovery-onboard skill includes a documented Vercel migration path.

### Agent Sandbox Alternatives

Agent sandboxes solve isolation: a safe box where a model's output can run. That box has no database, no production, no policy engine, and no rollback. Qovery is the layer after the sandbox.

- [The Best AI Coding Agent Sandboxes Compared](https://www.qovery.com/blog/best-ai-coding-agent-sandboxes-compared): E2B, CodeSandbox, Gitpod, Daytona and local Docker in one head-to-head, and where each stops short of a governed path to production.
- [All comparisons](https://www.qovery.com/alternatives): Where each platform stops and the execution layer begins.

## Migrations

Leaving a PaaS usually means moving onto somebody else's infrastructure again. These pages cover moving off Heroku, Render or Railway onto a cloud account the customer already owns, driven by an agent that reads the repository and produces a reviewable plan. Nothing in the process is destructive to the existing stack: both run in parallel until DNS moves, and DNS can move back.

- [Migrate to your own cloud](https://www.qovery.com/migrate): Hub for leaving Heroku, Render or Railway for AWS, Google Cloud, Azure or Scaleway. First app live in under an hour, full migration in days rather than quarters.
- [Heroku to AWS](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/heroku-to-aws): EKS, Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL and ElastiCache in the customer's own AWS account. Qovery is an AWS ISV Accelerate partner and is available on AWS Marketplace, so spend counts toward an EDP commitment. One team migrated 37 applications from Heroku to AWS in under two hours.
- [Heroku to Google Cloud](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/heroku-to-gcp): GKE, Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL and Memorystore in the customer's own project, where committed use and sustained use discounts apply and workloads reach BigQuery and Vertex AI over internal networking with Workload Identity.
- [Heroku to Azure](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/heroku-to-azure): AKS, Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Server and Azure Cache for Redis in the customer's own subscription. Spend counts toward an Enterprise Agreement or MACC commitment, and access is governed by Entra ID via SAML SSO.
- [Heroku to Scaleway](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/heroku-to-scaleway): Kapsule, Managed Database for PostgreSQL and Redis in EU data centres in Paris, Amsterdam or Warsaw. Scaleway is French-owned, so EU data carries no US CLOUD Act exposure. Usually the largest cost reduction of the four.
- [Render to AWS](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/render-to-aws): EKS, Amazon RDS and ElastiCache in the customer's own AWS account. The agent reads the existing render.yaml Blueprint to build the plan. Unlocks Savings Plans, Reserved Instances, Graviton and Spot, none of which a fixed Render instance type exposes.
- [Render to Google Cloud](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/render-to-gcp): GKE, Cloud SQL and Memorystore in the customer's own project. Custom machine types replace fixed instance tiers, sustained use discounts apply automatically, and every Google Cloud region is available rather than Render's five.
- [Render to Azure](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/render-to-azure): AKS, Azure Database for PostgreSQL and Azure Cache for Redis in the customer's own subscription. Entra ID SSO and audit logging without a plan gate - Render restricts SAML SSO and HIPAA workspaces to Scale and audit logs to Pro - and spend draws down an EA or MACC.
- [Railway to AWS](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/railway-to-aws): EKS, Amazon RDS and ElastiCache in the customer's own AWS account. The agent reads the existing railway.json. Replaces a flat usage meter with Savings Plans, Reserved Instances and Spot capacity for interruptible pools.
- [Railway to Google Cloud](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/railway-to-gcp): GKE, Cloud SQL and Memorystore in the customer's own project, with no per-plan ceiling on replicas, RAM, vCPU or volume size, and internal networking to BigQuery and Vertex AI via Workload Identity.
- [Railway to Azure](https://www.qovery.com/migrate/railway-to-azure): AKS in the customer's own subscription and virtual network - NSGs, private endpoints and peering, where Railway's private networking is Wireguard scoped to a single project environment. Entra ID governs deploys and spend draws down an EA or MACC.

